message.content:
{
  "summary": "This bill would create a non-binding, informative list of training requirements and opportunities established in state law for educators, school personnel, and volunteers at local education agencies (LEAs) and public charter schools. The list would categorize trainings based on whether they are required annually, every three years, before certain acts can be performed, or offered as opportunities.

Specifically, the bill would require that teachers, administrators, and other school personnel receive de-escalation training within their first year of employment and every three years thereafter. It would also require that school officials and employees working directly with students complete a child abuse training program within their first year of employment and every three years thereafter, with LEAs and public charter schools reporting compliance to the department of education. Additionally, the bill would require that teachers and counselors receive training on the LEA's policy prohibiting harassment, intimidation, bullying, or cyberbullying within their first year of employment and every three years thereafter.

The bill amends numerous existing statutes to note that their respective training requirements are included in this new compiled list. The bill would take effect on July 1, 2026."
}
